"On the number of simultaneous core partitions with $d$-distinct parts (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/326586607_On_the_number_of_simultaneous_core_partitions_with_d-distinct_parts)\nciteturn0search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; DOI:10.48550/arXiv.1807.08875 ... Our first main result is a proof of a recurrence relation conjectured by Sahin in 2018.\n\n# On the number of simultaneous core partitions with d-distinct parts\n\n  * July 2018\n\nDOI:10.48550/arXiv.1807.08875\n\nAuthors:\n\nNoah Kravitz\n\nNoah Kravitz\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nRequest file PDF\n\nTo read the file of this research, you can request a copy directly from the author.\n\nPreprints and early-stage research may not have been peer reviewed yet.\n\n## Abstract\n\nWe investigate the number $N_{d,r}(s)$ of $(s, s+r)$-core integer partitions with d-distinct parts. Our first main result is a proof of a recurrence relation conjectured by Sahin in 2018. We also derive generating functions, asymptotics, and exact formulas for $N_{d,r}(s)$ when r is within d of a multiple of s. Finally, we exhibit a surprising connection to A-restricted compositions.\n\n## No file available\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nTo read the file of this research,\nyou can request a copy directly from the author.\n\nRequest file PDF\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNeighbor-Locating Colorings in Graphs | ArxivLens (https://arxivlens.com/paperview/details/neighbor-locating-colorings-in-graphs-8787-2360708)\nciteturn0search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.4 years ago; Crawled: last month; @article{anon2018neighbor, title = {Neighbor-Locating Colorings in Graphs}, year = {2018}, eprint = {1806.11465}, archivePrefix = {arXiv}, primaryClass = {math.CO}, }\n\nBack ArXiv math.CO Neighbor-Locating Colorings in Graphs\n\nArXiv math.CO\n\n# Neighbor-Locating Colorings in Graphs\n\n1806.11465 Published Jul 2, 2018\n\nChat with paper Cite 中文 View PDF Share\n\n### Publication\n\nPublished: Jul 02, 2018\n\nCategories: math.CO\n\n### Metrics\n\nSource: ArXiv\n\n### AI Quick Summary\n\nThis paper establishes tight bounds for the neighbor-locating chromatic number of graphs, determining conditions under which a graph can have a neighbor-locating coloring with a specific number of colors, and examining how graph operations affect this property.\n\n### Paper Preview\n\n### Abstract\n\nA $k$-coloring of a graph $G$ is a $k$-partition $\\Pi=\\{S_1,\\ldots,S_k\\}$ of $V(G)$ into independent sets, called \\emph{colors}. A $k$-coloring is called \\emph{neighbor-locating} if for every pair of vertices $u,v$ belonging to the same color $S_i$, the set of colors of the neighborhood of $u$ is different from the set of colors of the neighborhood of $v$. The neighbor-locating chromatic number $\\chi _{_{NL}}(G)$ is the minimum cardinality of a neighbor-locating coloring of $G$. We establish some tight bounds for the neighbor-locating chromatic number of a graph, in terms of its order, maximum degree and independence number. We determine all connected graphs of order $n\\geq 5$ with neighbor-locating chromatic number $n$ or $n-1$. We examine the neighbor-locating chromatic number for two graph operations: join and disjoint union, and also for two graph families: split graphs and Mycielski graphs.\n\n### Paper Details\n\nPaper ID: 1806.11465\n\nLicense: http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\n\nComments: 20 pages, 4 figures\n\nCategories:\n\nmath.CO\n\nView on arXiv Download PDF\n\n### How to Cite This Paper\n\n[Button: BibTeX] [Button: APA] [Button: MLA] [Button: Chicago] [Button: IEEE]\n\n@article{anon2018neighbor, title = {Neighbor-Locating Colorings in Graphs}, year = {2018}, eprint = {1806.11465}, archivePrefix = {arXiv}, primaryClass = {math.CO}, }--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA note on matchings in abelian groups | Request PDF (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/327050455_A_note_on_matchings_in_abelian_groups)\nciteturn0search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 months ago; DOI:10.48550/arXiv.1808.04975 ... In this paper, we give a constructive approach to study the acyclic matchings in cyclic groups.\n\n# A note on matchings in abelian groups\n\n  * August 2018\n\nDOI:10.48550/arXiv.1808.04975\n\nAuthors:\n\nMohsen Aliabadi\n\nMohsen Aliabadi\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nShiva Soleimany Dizicheh\n\n  * University of Alberta\n\n\n## Abstract\n\nThe question of finding sets of monomials which are removable from a generic homogeneous polynomial through a linear change in its variables was raised by E. K. Wakeford in 1916. This linear algebra question motivated J. Losonczy to define the concept of acyclic matchings in Z n, and later in abelian groups. In this paper, we give a constructive approach to study the acyclic matchings in cyclic groups. We also introduce the notion of weakly matched subsets and investigate its relation with matchings in abelian groups.\n\n\n## No file available\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nTo read the file of this research,\nyou can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\nRequest file PDF\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nau:Gutierrez_M in:math - SciRate Search (https://scirate.com/search?q=au%3AGutierrez_M+in%3Amath)\nciteturn0search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago;   * Neighbor-Locating Colorings in Graphs ... Jul 02 2018 math.CO arXiv:1806.11465v1\n\n  * Neighbor-Locating Colorings in Graphs\n\nLiliana Alcon, Marisa Gutierrez, Carmen Hernando, Merce Mora, Ignacio M. Pelayo\n\nJul 02 2018 math.CO arXiv:1806.11465v1\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{1806.11465, author = {Liliana Alcon and Marisa Gutierrez and Carmen Hernando and Merce Mora and Ignacio M.~Pelayo}, title = {{N}ei