 $ are determined by their adjacency spectra, where $ s\\neq 2 $.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJava Based Distributed Learning Platform (https://www.davidpublisher.com/Public/uploads/Contribute/5b977e193bc0e.pdf)\nciteturn0search12 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 11 months ago; The following is the linear analogue of acyclicity for field extensions. ... In the following conjecture, the equivalent condition for the strong matchable vector spaces is questioned in group theory sense. ... “A Note on Acyclic Matchings in Abelian Groups.” https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.04975.\n\nConjecture 4. If A, B ⊆ Z/Zn are non-empty, |A| = |B| and A ∩ (A + B) = ∅, then there is an acyclic matching from A to B (here, n is assumed to be large enough).\n\nReferences\n\n[1] Losonczy, J. 1998. “On Matching in Groups.” Adv. in Appl. Math. 20: 385-91.\n\n[2] Aliabadi, M., Hadian, M., and Jafari, A. 2016. “On Matching Property in Groups and Vector Spaces.” J. Algebra Appl. 15 (1): 165001.\n\n[3] Aliabadi, M., and Janardhanan, M. J. “Onmatchable Subsets in Abelian Groups and Their Linear Analogues.” https://arxiv.org/pdf/1808.01376.\n\n[4] Aliabadi, M., and Dizicheh, S. S. “A Note on Acyclic Matchings in Abelian Groups.” https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.04975.\n\n[5] Aliabadi, M., and Janardhanan, M. V. 2018. “On Local Matching Property in Groups and Vector Spaces.” Australas. J. Combin. 70: 75-85.\n\n[6] Aliabadi, M., Jolany, H., Khajohnejad, A., Moghaddamzadeh, M. J., and Shahmohamad, H. 2017. “Acyclicity for Groups and Vector Spaces.” Southeast Asian Bulletin of Mathematics 41: 797-805.\n\n[7] Eliahou, S., and Lecouvey, C. 2010. “Mathching Subspaces in a Field Extension.” J. Algebra. 324: 3420-30.\n\n[8] Akbari, S., and Aliabadi, M. “Erratum to: Matching Subspaces in a Field Extensions.” arXiv: 1507.06983.\n\n[9] Aliabadi, M., and Darafsheh, M. R. 2013. “On Maximal and Minimal Linear Matching Property.” Algebra Discrete Math. 15 (2): 174-8.\n\n[10] Al